# Print command help for `z4x load` (`-z4x-cmd-load`).

eval "$_z4x_opt"

print -Pr -- "$(<<\END
%F{4}Usage:%f %F{2}z4x%f %Bload%b [-c|--compile] [--] [<dir>]...

Load plugins in Oh My Zsh or Prezto format, skipping over inexisting
directories. If %B-c%b or %B--compile%b is specified, plugin source files are
automatically compiled with %F{2}zcompile%f to speed up subsequent loading,
which boosts Zsh startup.

Relative directory names are resolved from %U$ZDOTDIR/%u, e.g., the command
below loads %U$ZDOTIDIR/plugins/bd%u:

  %F{2}z4x%f %Bload%b plugins/bd

Exit code of %F{2}z4x%f %Bload%b is that of sourcing the last plugin's
source file. Inexisting plugin directories do not affect exit code.
END
)"

# vim:ft=zsh
